WEBVTT

00:00:00.092 --> 00:00:02.962
This is the reference mock for the critique page.

00:00:03.276 --> 00:00:06.987
The design gives the photograph room to breathe, with the brief below

00:00:06.987 --> 00:00:08.909
it and feedback alongside it.

00:00:10.545 --> 00:00:14.757
Here is the working Angular page, using the same shoreline image.

00:00:15.072 --> 00:00:19.466
All critique text in this recording is a fixture, because no AI key

00:00:19.466 --> 00:00:20.534
is configured.

00:00:20.848 --> 00:00:25.611
The large image, compact status, restrained type, and comparison action

00:00:25.611 --> 00:00:26.692
follow the mock.

00:00:28.265 --> 00:00:29.872
What works comes first.

00:00:30.186 --> 00:00:34.293
Hovering an evidence loupe reveals the matching area of the photograph.

00:00:34.607 --> 00:00:38.857
The circular thumbnail is a real crop, and the spotlight helps connect

00:00:38.857 --> 00:00:41.267
each observation to visible detail.

00:00:42.852 --> 00:00:45.722
Click to pin a region while the pointer moves away.

00:00:46.036 --> 00:00:47.906
Escape clears the selection.

00:00:48.207 --> 00:00:52.852
Keyboard focus reveals the same evidence, so this interaction is available

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:53.985
without a mouse.

00:00:55.572 --> 00:00:58.074
Technical feedback follows the strengths.

00:00:58.375 --> 00:01:02.403
Exposure, focus, light, and colour stay grouped together.

00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:06.205
The image remains alongside the discussion as we scroll.

00:01:06.506 --> 00:01:11.205
Evidence without a location stays readable without an invented crop.

00:01:12.812 --> 00:01:17.299
Composition and story comes next, covering framing, separation,

00:01:17.299 --> 00:01:19.590
balance, hierarchy, and mood.

00:01:19.891 --> 00:01:23.958
The single column of observations keeps the critique easy to scan,

00:01:24.378 --> 00:01:25.998
matching the mock hierarchy.

00:01:27.625 --> 00:01:31.403
The top three improvements turn observations into actions.

00:01:31.704 --> 00:01:36.127
Each item explains what is visible, why it matters, and what to try.

00:01:36.441 --> 00:01:40.114
Evidence loupes still connect these priorities back to the frame.

00:01:41.705 --> 00:01:45.773
A boxed practice exercise suggests the next experiment.

00:01:46.087 --> 00:01:49.615
Personal notes remain separate from generated feedback.

00:01:49.929 --> 00:01:53.916
Here, saving a note updates the saved state without replacing the

00:01:53.916 --> 00:01:54.694
critique.

00:01:56.292 --> 00:01:58.952
Secondary actions live in the more menu.

00:01:59.266 --> 00:02:03.239
Regeneration requires confirmation, and the current critique stays

00:02:03.239 --> 00:02:06.123
available while a replacement runs or fails.

00:02:06.424 --> 00:02:09.149
Cancelling leaves the saved critique untouched.

00:02:10.732 --> 00:02:15.457
The primary action opens comparison with this photograph already selected.

00:02:15.772 --> 00:02:19.456
We choose a second fixture attempt to read both saved critiques side

00:02:19.456 --> 00:02:22.615
by side, without requesting new analysis.

00:02:24.212 --> 00:02:28.409
At mobile width, the heading, photograph, brief, and critique stack

00:02:28.409 --> 00:02:29.845
into one reading flow.

00:02:30.146 --> 00:02:34.646
The page fits the viewport without horizontal scrolling, and the circular

00:02:34.646 --> 00:02:36.872
evidence controls remain available.

00:02:38.465 --> 00:02:42.399
This tour demonstrated the real interface with clearly labelled fixture

00:02:42.399 --> 00:02:43.256
content.

00:02:43.557 --> 00:02:47.899
No AI request was made, and production Demo execution stays

00:02:47.899 --> 00:02:48.638
removed.

00:02:48.939 --> 00:02:52.217
A configured provider key enables real critiques.
